1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,638
Why do only your fingers and toes wrinkle in water?

2
00:00:03,938 --> 00:00:06,564
Your arms and your back stay smooth.

3
00:00:06,564 --> 00:00:09,626
Only fingertips and toes turn into prunes.

4
00:00:10,126 --> 00:00:13,201
Most people think the skin just soaks up water.

5
00:00:13,201 --> 00:00:14,967
That's not the whole story.

6
00:00:15,567 --> 00:00:19,586
In the 1930s, doctors noticed something strange.

7
00:00:19,586 --> 00:00:23,271
Fingers with a damaged nerve didn't wrinkle.

8
00:00:23,571 --> 00:00:25,307
Same skin, same water.

9
00:00:25,307 --> 00:00:27,595
No nerve signal, no wrinkles.

10
00:00:28,345 --> 00:00:30,187
Here's how it seems to work.

11
00:00:30,187 --> 00:00:33,937
The nerve tells blood vessels in the fingertip to narrow.

12
00:00:34,237 --> 00:00:39,605
The fingertip loses a little volume, and the skin on top folds into wrinkles.

13
00:00:40,355 --> 00:00:41,943
So it isn't just soaking.

14
00:00:41,943 --> 00:00:44,675
Your nervous system is making them wrinkle.

15
00:00:44,975 --> 00:00:45,243
Why?

16
00:00:45,243 --> 00:00:47,929
Scientists are still arguing about that.
